From 4693afff52cefdca36221252f19fad56edc79a0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin SAMSON <BEAVSN@BEA.local>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:50:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Clear only the copied rectangle, and widen lines along
 one axis like GX

A copy with clear started a render pass that cleared the whole target; GX
clears only the source rectangle. Super Mario Sunshine's level-start iris
copies and clears a 48x48 square at the centre each frame, so the screen
went black around that square. A partial copy now clears with a scissored
clear draw; a full-target copy keeps the pass load-clear.

Lines were widened perpendicular to their direction by the smaller of the
two viewport scales. GX widens them vertically when closer to horizontal,
horizontally otherwise, in EFB pixels. The iris masks the screen with one
horizontal line per row, and with a narrower horizontal scale rows showed
through as stripes.

